    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d874">

                <pb facs="1012" n="916" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg916"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">667.003/163: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the High Commissioner at
                        Constantinople</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-09T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1921—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>96. Your 272 November 21, 5 PM and your despatch 131 April 8, 1921.<anchor n="32"
                        xml:id="d874-f1"/> You may inform your Allied Colleagues that having in view
                    the present conditions at Constantinople, Department, as a temporary measure,
                    without prejudice to our rights and without establishing a precedent for any
                    other taxes, consents to Commissioner’s request that the municipal taxes
                    mentioned in your said despatch and stated to be necessary for the maintenance
                    of sanitary services be applied to American citizens with the understanding that
                    such services shall be under non-Turkish financial and technical supervision,
                    that the taxes shall be equally applied to all foreigners and that collection
                    shall be effected with the help of interallied police.</p>
                <p>Keep Department fully informed by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d874-f1" n="32" xml:id="d874-f1-content">
                <p>The latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
